It's phonetically impractical to get [h] between most vowels, because a cri=
terion for [h] is that there is no aerodynamically significant supraglottal=
 narrowing of stricture. So while [h] for /'/ in /e'e/ or /y'y/ is practica=
ble, [h] for /'/ in, say, /o'o/ or /u'u/ or /i'i/ is not (because the flank=
ing vowels create aerodynamically significant supraglottal stricture).

One can easily observe that [aha] and [axa] are rather easy to differentiat=
e, whereas /i'i/ and /ixi/ will be effectively indistinguishable (as [a=C3=
=A7a]) unless a very different allophone of /'/, such as [=CE=B8], is used.

--And.

